+# K1a quality harness inputs
+
+Implementation of Q0 r13 sections 1, 3 and 10 and the accepted T2b fetch
+specification. Harness tooling only; no product command, producer execution,
+measurement, adjudication result or qualification claim.
+
+Use the pinned Python with `-I -B`:
+
+```
+python3.14 -I -B tools/quality/corpus.py fetch --manifest MANIFEST --store STORE --temp-root PRIVATE_TMP --id ENTRY
+python3.14 -I -B tools/quality/corpus.py verify --manifest MANIFEST --store STORE --id ENTRY
+python3.14 -I -B tools/quality/corpus.py workspace --manifest MANIFEST --store STORE --workspaces WORKSPACES --id WORKSPACE
+python3.14 -I -B tools/quality/test_quality.py
+```
+
+Fetch reads Git objects without checkout, filters, hooks, submodule commands or
+LFS smudging. Git configuration and credentials are disabled. The session's
+owner forbids changing HOME; this implementation leaves HOME untouched and
+instead explicitly disables global/system Git configuration and supplies a
+private XDG configuration directory. Local acquisition requires `--local` and
+file URLs. No public corpus acquisition is needed to run the synthetic tests.
+
+The QD-22 digest streams the specified canonical array, without applying the
+record size limit to its preimage. Individual harness records retain CAN's
+4 MiB, depth, integer and exact-type limits. Stored trees are read-only and
+every reuse rehashes all bytes. Symlinks are never followed while hashing.
+
+Workspace assembly preserves the pinned overlay and renders the specified
+Cargo patches. npm and Python native rendering remains the discovery
+successor's open item; the result explicitly reports those undefined
+renderings. No package manager, installer or member file is invoked or edited.
+
+`records.py` supplies case-set admission, locked append-only ledgers, round
+freeze, input-based label compatibility and permanent exposure checks. The
+caller supplies all historical ledgers to the exposure check. These are
+libraries for K1b/K1c and K2, not a vote or qualification engine. A torn ledger
+refuses further append; it is not truncated or repaired.
+
+Owner sign-offs D3, D12 and D13 remain open. These input mechanisms make no
+selection, runner or qualification decision on the owner's behalf.
